# QA replay of a Tasks screenshot's reading (owner, 2026-10-19: from a panel of four, B, "OPERATIONAL rows where the
# map's work is"; after trying the dev build the same day, "sorted on top of the list always as they are time-sensitive"
# and "the same animation as the other quests"): the reading's cue lists every task read, one animation for all of them,
# and the rows it brought glow in on the rail; a task that runs out leaves the ended line; Shoreline's kill without a
# countdown says its reading's age; Woods' line of no known kind has the generic glyph; then a Streets raid whose
# survival ends before the raid could. Drafted by the UI QA pass of 2026-10-19. A developer build plays it with
# --dev-view --dev-script; how to run it, and what each still must show: operational-feedback.md beside this file.
# Times are in seconds.

# A --dev-view session starts on settings of its own, as at a first start, so the tour opened by itself at chapter 1
# once the data was there. It ends first.
tour end
map streets-of-tarkov
wait 3

# The Tasks screen's OPERATIONAL table as a screenshot taken now shows it: five made-up tasks and one that runs out 3 s
# later (a survival on Streets ending in 25 min, a kill on Customs, a weekly's two hand-overs on any map, a kill on
# Shoreline without a countdown, a line of no known kind on Woods; the file isn't written this run).
tasks 5 ended
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\operational-feedback\t0
# The cue whole: its title decoded, its six rows risen in, the one that ends soonest first (from about 1.6 s; the wait
# keeps to it with the snapshot step of 2026-10-26, the developer view's tabs taken while the script goes on).
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\operational-feedback\cue
# The sixth task has run out by the next still, and the cue has gone.
wait 4
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\operational-feedback\t1

# The other maps' cards, looked at without choosing them.
map shoreline look
wait 2
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\operational-feedback\shoreline
map woods look
wait 2
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\operational-feedback\woods

# A PMC raid on Streets: the raid card's OPERATIONAL, its survival ending before the raid could.
map streets-of-tarkov
wait 2
load
steps
start
wait 3
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\operational-feedback\raid-start
exit
